  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\u27f6[\\begin{aligned}4x+7y \\\\ 8y-5x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
  "worked_solution": "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\u27f6[\\begin{aligned}4x+7y \\\\ -5x+8y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4x+7y \\\\ -5x+8y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4x+7y \\\\ -5x+8y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
